From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: AKM suite copy takes a count, not a byte length
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

num_akms counts selectors, not bytes - it is the attribute length divided by
sizeof(uint32_t) a few lines above. ap_akms and sta_akms are
uint32_t[WIFI_NUM_AKM_SUITES] (wifidefs.h), so copying num_akms bytes moved a
quarter of the data and left the rest of the destination as it was: three
advertised AKM suites became 3 bytes instead of 12.

Silent on MT7996 today. The driver does not report
NL80211_ATTR_IFTYPE_AKM_SUITES at all, so this branch never runs and the arrays
stay empty - measured 2026-09-03, ubus call wifi.radio.radio0 status returns
"ap_akms": [] and "sta_akms": []. The agent therefore falls back to the UCI
encryption options and the corruption never shows.

That is exactly why it is worth fixing now: the moment any driver does report
them, the AKM Suite Capabilities TLV goes out with a quarter of one selector
and whatever was in the array before, and the fault would be looked for in the
TLV writer rather than here.

Also clamp to the destination. The count comes from the kernel while the arrays
are fixed size, and nothing between the two checks it. ARRAY_SIZE keeps this
independent of the constant's name; both arrays have the same length.

--- a/libwifi/modules/nl80211/nlwifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/nl80211/nlwifi.c
@@ -2631,12 +2631,40 @@
 			akms = nla_data(tbk[NL80211_IFTYPE_AKM_ATTR_SUITES]);
 			num_akms = nla_len(tbk[NL80211_IFTYPE_AKM_ATTR_SUITES]) / sizeof(uint32_t);
 
+			/* num_akms counts selectors, not bytes: it is the
+			 * attribute length divided by sizeof(uint32_t) just
+			 * above. ap_akms and sta_akms are uint32_t arrays, so
+			 * copying num_akms bytes moved a quarter of the data
+			 * and left the rest of the destination as it was -
+			 * three advertised AKM suites became 3 bytes instead
+			 * of 12.
+			 *
+			 * Silent on MT7996 today: the driver does not report
+			 * NL80211_ATTR_IFTYPE_AKM_SUITES at all, so this whole
+			 * branch never runs and ap_akms stays empty (measured
+			 * 2026-09-03: ubus call wifi.radio.radio0 status gives
+			 * "ap_akms": []). The agent therefore falls back to the
+			 * UCI encryption options. The moment a driver does
+			 * report them, the AKM Suite Capabilities TLV would go
+			 * out corrupted and the fault would be looked for in
+			 * the TLV writer, not here.
+			 *
+			 * Clamp to the destination as well: the count comes
+			 * from the kernel, but ap_akms and sta_akms are
+			 * uint32_t[WIFI_NUM_AKM_SUITES] (wifidefs.h) and both
+			 * have the same length.
+			 */
+			if (num_akms > (int)ARRAY_SIZE(radio->ap_akms))
+				num_akms = (int)ARRAY_SIZE(radio->ap_akms);
+
 			nla_for_each_nested(nliftype, tbk[NL80211_IFTYPE_AKM_ATTR_IFTYPES], i) {
 				if (nla_type(nliftype) == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) {
-					memcpy(radio->ap_akms, akms, num_akms);
+					memcpy(radio->ap_akms, akms,
+					       num_akms * sizeof(*radio->ap_akms));
 					radio->num_ap_akms = num_akms;
 				} else if (nla_type(nliftype) == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) {
-					memcpy(radio->sta_akms, akms, num_akms);
+					memcpy(radio->sta_akms, akms,
+					       num_akms * sizeof(*radio->sta_akms));
 					radio->num_sta_akms = num_akms;
 				}
 			}
